course: dictionary
lesson: 10119
title: Thorny: sharp plants and tricky problems
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have two meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «Move carefully near thorny bushes such as roses and brambles» is about plants with sharp points, so here thorny means having thorns.
explain: Now read «a thorny problem». A problem cannot have sharp points, so try the other meaning: difficult and complicated, the sort of problem people argue about. Always ask what the word is describing, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Thorny is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a bush, an issue or a problem. Like many adjectives, it can change its ending to compare things: thorny, thornier, thorniest.
fact: Thorny has two meanings: having thorns, and difficult to solve.
fact: Thorns are sharp, pointed parts on a stem or branch, as on roses and brambles.
fact: «A thorny issue» is a hard question that people argue about.
fact: «The Australian thorny devil» eats thousands of small ants at one meal and shows a spiny false head to predators.
fact: Camels really do eat thorny desert plants, because their tough lips and mouths are not hurt by the thorns.
exercise: «Move carefully near thorny bushes such as roses and brambles.» What does thorny mean here? | Difficult to solve | Very quiet | *Having sharp, pointed thorns | Wet and grey
exercise: «It was a thorny problem that the whole class argued about.» What does thorny mean here? | Very small | Covered in bright leaves | *Difficult and likely to cause arguments | Happy and cheerful
exercise: Sam says a thorny issue must be a plant. What is the best reply? | *No, it can mean a hard question that people argue about | No, it means a sunny day | Yes, it means a sharp knife | Yes, it is always a plant
test: «The thorny question kept the meeting going for hours.» What does thorny mean here? | Soft and warm | Bright and glowing | *Difficult and likely to cause arguments | Sharp and prickly
test: Which of these is most likely to be thorny? | A soft cushion | *A bramble bush | A cold, grey sea | A calm, sunny lawn
exam: Which sentence uses thorny in its plant meaning? | «We had a thorny talk about the rules.» | «The thorny homework took an hour.» | *«Mind the thorny rose bush by the gate.»
